From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: M5Stack Agent <agent@m5stack.local>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: model Cardputer ADV panel rotation

M5GFX configures the ST7789 as a 135x240 panel with 52/40 controller
offsets and starts it at rotation 1. The QEMU model used a 320x240 memory
crop with the offsets swapped and MADCTL disabled, so portrait applications
such as Piano Tiles appeared in only the left part of the framebuffer.

Keep the controller memory in its native 240x320 orientation, apply the
guest MADCTL, and rotate the glass into the board's 240x135 physical frame.
This preserves the fixed display probe while allowing both M5GFX rotation 0
and rotation 1 to render the complete panel.
---
 hw/m5stopwatch/m5cardputeradv.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/m5stopwatch/m5cardputeradv.c b/hw/m5stopwatch/m5cardputeradv.c
--- a/hw/m5stopwatch/m5cardputeradv.c
+++ b/hw/m5stopwatch/m5cardputeradv.c
@@ -74,14 +74,15 @@ void m5cardputeradv_board_init(MemoryRegion *sys_mem, DeviceState *intmatrix,
                                 ETS_SPI3_INTR_SOURCE);
 
     DeviceState *panel = qdev_new(TYPE_M5_SPI_PANEL);
-    qdev_prop_set_uint32(panel, "mem-width", 320);
-    qdev_prop_set_uint32(panel, "mem-height", 240);
+    qdev_prop_set_uint32(panel, "mem-width", 240);
+    qdev_prop_set_uint32(panel, "mem-height", 320);
     qdev_prop_set_uint32(panel, "vis-width", 240);
     qdev_prop_set_uint32(panel, "vis-height", 135);
-    qdev_prop_set_uint32(panel, "offset-x", 40);
-    qdev_prop_set_uint32(panel, "offset-y", 53);
+    qdev_prop_set_uint32(panel, "offset-x", 52);
+    qdev_prop_set_uint32(panel, "offset-y", 40);
     qdev_prop_set_uint32(panel, "read-id", 0x00000081);
-    qdev_prop_set_bit(panel, "apply-madctl", false);
+    qdev_prop_set_uint32(panel, "glass-rotation", 1);
+    qdev_prop_set_bit(panel, "apply-madctl", true);
     qdev_prop_set_bit(panel, "keyboard", true);
     qdev_prop_set_bit(panel, "invert", true);
     qdev_realize_and_unref(panel, NULL, &error_fatal);
